{
 "_comment": [
  "The test suite as scope shards. Generated into .gatehouse/gates/test-*.json and pipeline.writ by",
  "scripts/gatehouse-test-shards.py; `--check` refuses a stale generation. Layout measured on nucleus",
  "2fc73eda over the 40 merged PRs before it (gatehouse docs/sublinear-testing.md): two shards beat",
  "more, because each run pays ~130 s of per-attempt overhead against a 101 s suite.",
  "fixtures: paths a package's tests read OUTSIDE its dependency closure, from strace of every test",
  "process (open/exec/stat of a file, directory listings as dir/**, probes of absent paths whose",
  "parent exists), rustc dep-info and build-script rerun-if-changed. The four bare lib.rs/main.rs",
  "entries are proptest's search for a crate root; .env/.ssh are probes the tests make.",
  "Compile-time reads come from rustc's dep-info, NORMALIZED: include_str!(\"../../../examples/x\") is recorded as written, `..` and all, and only normpath shows it leaves the crate (the shadow caught the one the first derivation missed, as a compile error)."
 ],
